s://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-24T21:15:04Z","updated_at":"2021-08-24T21:15:30Z","body":"I'm running into issues with this as well. All other pages seem to work with lots of DBs except the home page, which absolutely tanks. Would be willing to put some work into this, if there's been any kind of progress on concepts on how this ought to work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/904982056/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905899177","html_url":"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/issues/859#issuecomment-905899177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/859","id":905899177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBm6k_c41_uyp","user":{"login":"brandonrobertz","id":2670795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzA3OTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2670795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz","html_url":"https://github.com/brandonrobertz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-25T21:48:00Z","updated_at":"2021-08-25T21:48:00Z","body":"Upon first stab, there's two issues here:\r\n- DB/table/row counts (as discussed above). This isn't too bad if the DBs are actually above the MAX limit check.\r\n- Populating the internal DB. On first load of a giant set of DBs, it can take 10-20 mins to populate. By altering datasette and persisting the internal DB to disk, this problem is vastly improved, but I'm sure this will cause problems elsewhere.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905899177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905900807","html_url":"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/issues/859#issuecomment-905900807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/859","id":905900807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBm6k_c41_vMH","user":{"login":"simonw","id":9599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw","html_url":"https://github.com/simonw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simonw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-25T21:51:10Z","updated_at":"2021-08-25T21:51:10Z","body":"10-20 minutes to populate `_internal`! How many databases and tables is that for?\r\n\r\nI may have to rethink the `_internal` mechanism entirely. One possible alternative would be for the Datasette homepage to just show a list of available databases (maybe only if there are more than X connected) and then load in their metadata only the first time they are accessed.\r\n\r\nI need to get my own stress testing rig setup for this.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905900807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905904540","html_url":"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/issues/859#issuecomment-905904540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/859","id":905904540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBm6k_c41_wGc","user":{"login":"brandonrobertz","id":2670795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzA3OTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2670795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz","html_url":"https://github.com/brandonrobertz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonrobertz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-25T21:59:14Z","updated_at":"2021-08-25T21:59:55Z","body":"I did two tests: one with 1000 5-30mb DBs and a second with 20 multi gig DBs. For the second, I created them like so:\r\n`for i in {1..20}; do sqlite-generate db$i.db --tables ${i}00 --rows 100,2000 --columns 5,100 --pks 0 --fks 0; done`\r\n\r\nThis was for deciding whether to use lots of small DBs or to group things into a smaller number of bigger DBs. The second strategy wins.\r\n\r\nBy simply persisting the `_internal` DB to disk, I was able to avoid most of the performance issues I was experiencing previously. (To do this, I changed the `datasette/internal_db.py:init_internal_db` creates to if not exists, and changed the `_internal` DB instantiation in `datasette/app.py:Datasette.__init__` to a path with `is_mutable=True`.) Super rough, but the pages now load so I can continue testing ideas.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/simonw/datasette/issues/comments/905904540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]